        67.39069366455078,
        527.1729736328125,
        81.83369445800781
      ],
      "text": "Data reviewed from TMC207-C211 corresponded to children aged 5–18 years and data from IMPAACT",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.948881149291992,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        80.59070587158203,
        527.4376831054688,
        95.03370666503906
      ],
      "text": "P1108 included children aged 0–6 years; therefore, the review of pharmacokinetics and safety data",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        93.79071807861328,
        527.5389404296875,
        108.23371887207031
      ],
      "text": "focused mainly on data from IMPAACT P1108. Although the sample size of the available interim",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        105.71472930908203,
        527.4063110351562,
        121.43373107910156
      ],
      "text": "n data for review was small ( =12), the GDG 2021 concluded that in children aged 0–6 years, cardiac",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        120.19074249267578,
        527.4034423828125,
        134.6337432861328
      ],
      "text": "safety signals were not distinct from those reported in adults. Population pharmacokinetic models",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        133.3907012939453,
        527.4069213867188,
        147.8336944580078
      ],
      "text": "from both studies suggest that drug exposures observed in adults can be reached in most children",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        146.59071350097656,
        527.382568359375,
        161.03370666503906
      ],
      "text": "receiving bedaquiline, although some dose modification may be necessary depending on the age",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        159.7907257080078,
        181.48431396484375,
        174.2337188720703
      ],
      "text": "and weight of the child.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        181.49464416503906,
        527.3445434570312,
        195.93763732910156
      ],
      "text": "In addition, data from a paediatric MDR/RR-TB IPD were analysed descriptively (24 231 records from all",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.954004287719727,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        194.69459533691406,
        527.3695068359375,
        209.13758850097656
      ],
      "text": "six WHO regions, the majority from India and South Africa). The search was conducted in April 2020.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        207.8946075439453,
        527.4591674804688,
        222.3376007080078
      ],
      "text": "Just under 20 000 of these records were used for a matched analysis of treatment outcomes in children",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.95942497253418,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        221.09474182128906,
        527.385009765625,
        235.53773498535156
      ],
      "text": "being treated for DR-TB. The analysis included 40 children aged below 6 years and 68 children aged",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        234.29469299316406,
        527.1116333007812,
        248.73768615722656
      ],
      "text": "6–12 years who received bedaquiline. In the matched analysis, bedaquiline was significantly associated",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.962786674499512,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        247.4947052001953,
        527.3782958984375,
        261.9377136230469
      ],
      "text": "with shorter treatment duration and a lower aOR of injectable TB drug use. There was no statistically",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        260.6947021484375,
        527.5447998046875,
        275.1377258300781
      ],
      "text": "significant difference in successful treatment outcomes between children aged below 6 years receiving",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.965596199035645,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        272.61859130859375,
        527.396240234375,
        288.3376159667969
      ],
      "text": "P an all-oral bedaquiline-based regimen and those not receiving bedaquiline (89% versus 97%,  =0.9).",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 10.988444328308105,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        287.0947265625,
        457.5513916015625,
        301.5377502441406
      ],
      "text": "Residual confounding (including confounding by indication) was thought to be likely.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        308.798583984375,
        527.603759765625,
        323.2416076660156
      ],
      "text": "A child-friendly formulation of bedaquiline (20 mg scored uncoated tablet) is being used in the",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        321.99859619140625,
        527.3795776367188,
        336.4416198730469
      ],
      "text": "Janssen C211 study to dose children aged below 5 years and will also soon be used in an updated",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        335.1986083984375,
        527.3739624023438,
        349.6416320800781
      ],
      "text": "protocol of the IMPAACT study P1108 (to date, this study has used the 100 mg formulation in all age",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        348.39862060546875,
        527.4268188476562,
        362.8416442871094
      ],
      "text": "groups). No head-to-head studies were conducted to examine the bioequivalence of the 20 mg and",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        361.5986022949219,
        527.4810180664062,
        376.0416259765625
      ],
      "text": "the 100 mg formulation of bedaquiline. Indirect bioequivalence testing showed that both tablets have",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.979631423950195,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        374.7986145019531,
        527.4409790039062,
        389.24163818359375
      ],
      "text": "the same bioavailability and can be used interchangeably at the same total dose. Findings from the",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        386.72259521484375,
        527.4089965820312,
        402.4416198730469
      ],
      "text": "(78) bedaquiline crush study   also showed that the bioavailability of bedaquiline tablets suspended in",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        401.1986083984375,
        305.9581604003906,
        415.6416320800781
      ],
      "text": "water was the same as for tablets swallowed whole.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        426.0099182128906,
        503.1022644042969,
        440.3648986816406
      ],
      "text": "PICO question 2–2021 (Childhood TB, 2021) (use of delamanid in MDR/RR-TB patients",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiBold",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        441.0099182128906,
        170.75048828125,
        455.3648986816406
      ],
      "text": "aged below 3 years)",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiBold",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        462.82379150390625,
        527.374755859375,
        477.2668151855469
      ],
      "text": "To answer the PICO question on the use of delamanid in children aged below 3 years, data were",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        476.0238037109375,
        527.4222412109375,
        490.4668273925781
      ],
      "text": "reviewed by the GDG 2021 from a Phase 1, open-label, age de-escalation trial designed to assess",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        489.22381591796875,
        527.4354248046875,
        503.6668395996094
      ],
      "text": "the pharmacokinetics, safety and tolerability of delamanid administered twice daily for 10 days in",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        502.423828125,
        524.4015502929688,
        516.8668212890625
      ],
      "text": "children with MDR/RR-TB on treatment with an optimized background regimen (protocol 242–12–",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        515.623779296875,
        527.4188232421875,
        530.0667724609375
      ],
      "text": "232)  and from the corresponding open-label extension study (protocol 242–12–233).  Data from  43 44",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        528.8237915039062,
        527.4441528320312,
        543.2667846679688
      ],
      "text": "cohorts 1 (age 12–17 years), 2 (age 6–11 years), 3 (age 3–5 years) and 4 (age 0–2 years) for both",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        542.0238037109375,
        527.3904418945312,
        556.466796875
      ],
      "text": "protocols were reviewed. Exposures in the 0–2-year age group were lower than those of children",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        555.2238159179688,
        527.14208984375,
        569.6668090820312
      ],
      "text": "aged 3 years and older, necessitating a modelling or simulation approach to dosing. No cardiac safety",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.97512149810791,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        568.423828125,
        527.3958740234375,
        582.8668212890625
      ],
      "text": "signals distinct from those reported in adults were observed in children aged 0–2 years. However,",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        581.623779296875,
        527.33984375,
        596.0667724609375
      ],
      "text": "consideration of these findings should take into account that children had lower drug exposures",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        594.8237915039062,
        527.4125366210938,
        609.2667846679688
      ],
      "text": "than adults. Pharmacodynamic simulations suggested that clinically meaningful changes in QT (i.e.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        608.0238037109375,
        527.4100952148438,
        622.466796875
      ],
      "text": "prolongation) would be unlikely in children aged below 3 years, even if higher doses were used to",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        621.2238159179688,
        355.76177978515625,
        635.6668090820312
      ],
      "text": "reach drug exposures comparable to those achieved in adults.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        642.927734375,
        527.2159423828125,
        657.3707275390625
      ],
      "text": "CNS effects (paraesthesia, tremors, anxiety, depression and insomnia) were included in the delamanid",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.981284141540527,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        656.127685546875,
        527.48779296875,
        670.5706787109375
      ],
      "text": "label for both adults and children as important potential safety concerns for the drug. In March 2021,",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.992847442626953,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        669.3278198242188,
        527.4268188476562,
        683.7708129882812
      ],
      "text": "the study sponsor released a statement of intent to modify the labelling to include hallucinations as",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        682.52783203125,
        527.1153564453125,
        696.9708251953125
      ],
      "text": "an adverse reaction. This new safety signal has been more prevalent among children than adults, with",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.9822359085083,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
